# PORTFOLIO OVERHAUL — CHANGES MADE (SUMMARY)

> This file replaces the previous `issues.context` recruiter-audit directive. That directive proposed 21 points; each was independently verified against the live code before acting on it — several turned out to be stale or inaccurate (noted below). The changes actually implemented were decided interactively with the site owner, section by section, and this document records what was actually done, not what was originally proposed.

---

## 01 · Hero (`src/components/sections/hero.tsx`)
- Mobile skill-badge text bumped from 9px → 11px (desktop was already 12px, unaffected).
- Consolidated the duplicate mobile-tag rendering: the live mobile fallback badges (previously `text-[8.5px] sm:text-[10px]`) bumped to `text-[10px] sm:text-[11px]` and bolded.
- Bolded the 7 desktop skill tags (Workflow Automation, Product Strategy, User Research, Roadmapping, System Design, Product Discovery, Storytelling) and all 6 mobile tags — applied via a single shared class change so both canvas paths stay in sync.
- Bolded the "Best Work / Side Projects / Contact" quick-links in the top metadata bar.

## 02 · Table of Contents (`src/components/sections/nav-index.tsx`, `data.ts`)
- Shortened the cursive "quick note" sticky from a 16-word sentence to "Short on time? Jump to Best Work."
- Removed the "Directly click on the section name you want to inspect." instruction line entirely.

## 03 · Scrolling ticker (`src/components/sections/brand-marquee.tsx`)
- Fixed a data/render mismatch: the ticker now reads from `MARQUEE_ITEMS` in `data.ts` instead of a hardcoded, disconnected local array. No visual change; future content edits now actually take effect.

## 04 · "The Beginning" (`src/components/sections/origin.tsx`, `data.ts`)
- Replaced the 32-word cursive sentence heading with a one-line subtitle: "From engineering foundations to product leadership."
- Replaced the 3 dense paragraphs with 3 short, bolded bullets (Education & Curiosity / The Research Click / The Pivot to Product), grounded in the original resume copy.
- Removed the large cursive headline entirely (per later request) and removed the "PRODUCT ROADMAP? / plans changed." motif stamp entirely (distracting, unnecessary).
- The mobile heading/motif-overlap issue is moot now that both elements are gone.

## 05 · Career Metro (`src/components/sections/best-work-metro.tsx`) — full rebuild
- Replaced the scroll-driven GSAP `ScrollTrigger` pin with a normal-flow, timer-driven auto-advancing carousel: advances every 6s, pauses instantly on hover or any manual interaction, resumes 4s after the last interaction.
- Added visible Prev/Next buttons; rewired the existing station dots and keyboard arrow/Home/End nav to a single `goToStation` state mutator shared with autoplay.
- Autoplay pauses while the deep-dive case-study modal is open and never runs for reduced-motion or mobile users (mobile stacked cards are untouched).
- **Bug found and fixed post-implementation** (caught via the site owner's live testing): the initial track tween used `xPercent`, which GSAP resolves against the track's own total width (600% for 6 panels), not the viewport — causing massive overshoot and the "black sliding portion" / erratic-jump behavior reported. Fixed by switching to pixel-based `x` translation (`-activeIndex * panelWidth`), verified pixel-exact via direct DOM/transform inspection and a rapid-click repro test matching the reported bug.
- A follow-on fix to the above (a `max-w-2xl` cap added to the panel itself) broke the uniform-panel-width assumption the pixel math depends on; corrected by moving the width cap to an inner content wrapper instead, keeping the outer panel at a clean `w-full`.
- Station content (heading + Step Out button) is now centered as a unit within each full-width panel instead of left-hugging with a large empty gap on the right (station panels are wider now that the 850px cap was removed for correct tweening).
- Reversed the bottom photo marquee's scroll direction from right-to-left to left-to-right per request.

## 06 · Published Work (`src/components/sections/research-archive.tsx`, `data.ts`)
- Removed the long sentence heading entirely — just the "Published Work" title remains.
- Bolded the supervisor name and institution on each paper card.
- Removed the category tags from every paper card (contrast claim from the old audit was stale — metadata was already legible, no change needed there).

## 07 · Product Lab (`src/components/sections/product-lab.tsx`, `data.ts`)
- Deleted the entire unused "44-word collage + 10 skill-tag hover preview" system (`WORD_SPECS`, `PREVIEWS`, `POSITIONS`, related state/handlers) — it was fully coded but never rendered, and had a latent bug (3 of 10 tags had no matching hover shape). Previewed for the site owner, who did not want the design; removed rather than fixed.
- Removed the category-chip tags from the 4 side-project cards. Side-project cards, links, and status badges are otherwise unchanged.

## 08 · Honors & Recognition (`src/components/sections/achievements.tsx`, `data.ts`)
- Removed the "MILESTONES AND RECOGNITIONS EARNED ALONG THE WAY." sentence entirely. Title stays "Honors & Recognition."

## 09 · Contact (`src/components/sections/contact.tsx`, `data.ts`, `src/components/shell/scroll-to-top.tsx`)
- Added a click-to-reveal phone button (`tel:` link) and a "View Detailed Résumé ↗" CTA + closing message, alongside existing email/LinkedIn/GitHub.
- Moved the floating "scroll to top" button from bottom-left to bottom-right — it was overlapping the "Pankaj Gupta" signature in the footer on mobile.

## Cross-cutting
- Added a reusable `renderBold()` helper (`_shared.tsx`) that parses `**text**` into `<strong>` — used across Origin, Achievements-adjacent copy, and Research Archive metadata.
- `SectionShell` consolidation was scoped down after investigation: `SectionShell` is hardcoded for dark/black sections. Origin and Achievements are paper (light) sections, so forcing them onto it would have broken their colors — matching an existing pattern already established in `research-archive.tsx`, which hand-rolls a paper-safe equivalent instead of using `SectionShell` directly. Left as-is to avoid a visual regression.

## Verification performed
- `npm run build` — compiles successfully.
- `npx tsc --noEmit` — zero new type errors introduced (8 pre-existing errors confirmed via git stash comparison, unrelated to this work: `achievements.tsx` SFX type, `best-work-metro.tsx` missing `extras` field on `MetroStation`, `hero.tsx` undefined `addNewNode` in the dev-only Studio editor).
- Dev server compiled cleanly through every edit (checked after each file).
- Metro carousel functionally verified in-browser: autoplay cadence, pause-on-interaction, and dot/button navigation all confirmed correct.

---

# ROUND 2 — FOLLOW-UP REFINEMENTS

A further round of section-by-section feedback after Round 1 shipped. Same verification discipline (build + `tsc --noEmit` + in-browser DOM checks after each change).

## 10 · Contact action card (`contact.tsx`, `data.ts`)
- Reordered/simplified to: **Email Me** (copies address, no icon, no `mailto:` redirect) → **Reveal Phone Number** → **View Detailed Resume**.
- Removed the arrow (↗) and the accented "Résumé" spelling — plain "Resume", no arrow.
- Removed the "No Forms, No Funnels, No Friction" annotation line entirely (also removed `CONTACT.annotation` from `data.ts`).
- On mobile, moved LinkedIn/GitHub links to sit *below* the action card (was above) via independent `order-*` grid classes, decoupled from the desktop column layout.

## 11 · Footer (`contact.tsx`)
- Removed the blinking cursor next to the "Pankaj Gupta" signature.
- On mobile, the return-to-top control now splits: a standalone arrow button sits on the **left** edge of the footer, while the signature + "Return to Top" text sit on the **right**. Desktop keeps one inline arrow+label button, unchanged.
- Fixed a duplicate-control bug this split briefly introduced: the global floating scroll-to-top button (bottom-right, `scroll-to-top.tsx`) now hides via `IntersectionObserver` once the footer is in view, so only one scroll-to-top control is ever visible at a time.

## 12 · Achievements education strip (`achievements.tsx`)
- Centered the school-name headers (DTU / IIIT Delhi / NYU) on mobile only; the left-border-rail + left-aligned layout is preserved from `sm:` up.

## 13 · Table of Contents → Brand Marquee spacing (`nav-index.tsx`)
- Tightened the gap between the last TOC item and the ticker below it (asymmetric `pt-*`/`pb-*` split instead of symmetric padding). Verified 0px stray gap via DOM measurement.

## 14 · Brand Marquee (`brand-marquee.tsx`, `data.ts`)
- `MARQUEE_ITEMS` reverted back to the original PM-methodology keyword list (Rapid Prototyping, Product Discovery, Market Research, etc.) per site-owner preference — a prior edit had replaced it with a shorter, less representative list.
- Removed scroll-velocity-driven direction reversal: the ticker now always scrolls left-to-right regardless of scroll direction; only its *speed* still reacts to scroll velocity.

## 15 · Origin → Brand Marquee gap (`origin.tsx`)
- Reduced the top padding to close the visible gap between the ticker and the "01 / THE BEGINNING" section start. Verified 0px stray gap via DOM measurement.

## 16 · Career Metro spacing (`best-work-metro.tsx`)
- Switched the station panel from vertically-centered content to top-aligned content, then tuned top padding directly — the previous centered layout made the route-bar-to-"PLATFORM 0X" gap a side effect of content height rather than a controllable value. Gap reduced from ~114px to a consistent ~30px across all stations, verified with no overlap into the bottom photo marquee (checked across 5 stations, up to 412px of content height).

## 17 · Dead-code sweep (repo-wide)
Removed code confirmed to have zero live references (verified via grep + build + `tsc --noEmit` before and after):
- `contact.tsx`: unused `ArrowRight` icon import (left over from the deleted magnetic-CTA cluster).
- `origin.tsx`: a dead GSAP `ScrollTrigger` SVG-path-draw effect whose `pathRef` was never attached to any DOM element — it ran against `null` on every render and did nothing. Removed the effect, `PATH_D`, `ANNOTATION_POSITIONS`, and the now-unused `gsap`/`ScrollTrigger`/`useRef`/`useEffect` imports.
- `best-work-metro.tsx`: an unreachable `station.extras` render block — no station in `METRO_STATIONS` ever sets `.extras` (it isn't even part of the `MetroStation` type), so this was a pre-existing dead branch *and* a pre-existing TypeScript error. Deleting it fixed 3 of the session's 8 baseline TS errors.
- `search-index.ts` / `command-palette.tsx`: the "work experiences" command-palette search entries pointed at `target: "work-log"`, an element id that doesn't exist anywhere in the DOM — clicking one silently did nothing. Removed the dead search-entry generator along with the now-fully-unused `EXPERIENCES` array and `Experience` type in `data.ts` (~110 lines).
- `data.ts`: trimmed to only the fields each consuming component actually reads — removed `IDENTITY` (unused anywhere), `CASE_CLOSE` (unused anywhere), `PHILOSOPHY_QUOTE` (its only consumer was an orphaned file, see below), and unused fields on `PRELOADER`, `ORIGIN`, `METRO_INTRO`, `RESEARCH`, `LAB`, `CONTACT`.
- Deleted 6 orphaned files never imported by anything in the render tree: `philosophy-quote.tsx`, `shortcuts-overlay.tsx` + its sole dependent hook `use-keyboard-shortcuts.ts` (fully built "?" shortcuts-help panel with no trigger anywhere — `keyboard-router.tsx` only wires ⌘K), `shortcut-hint.tsx` (already a stub, its own comment says "permanently removed per user directive"), `session-stats-hud.tsx` and `side-rail.tsx` (decorative widgets whose underlying tracking/data hooks stay live via other, actually-rendered components).
- **Exception, not deleted**: `mute-toggle.tsx` was also unrendered, but its backing state (`useMuteStore`) is actively wired into `sound-manager.tsx` and gates every `play()` call site-wide — meaning sound was playing throughout the site with no way for a visitor to mute it. Flagged to the site owner, who chose to re-add the button rather than delete it; it's now wired into `page.tsx` (bottom-left, matching its own original styling).

## Verification performed (Round 2)
- `npm run build` — compiles successfully after every change.
- `npx tsc --noEmit` — 5 errors remain, all pre-existing and unrelated (down from 8; the 3 fixed were the `station.extras` dead block above).
- Dev server restarted clean (fresh `.next` cache) after the data.ts/search-index.ts edits to rule out stale Turbopack HMR state; confirmed via server log + DOM inspection that the build is genuinely error-free, not just visually appearing to work.
- In-browser DOM verification for every spacing/layout change (gap measurements via `getBoundingClientRect`), plus functional checks: footer arrow click scrolls to top, mute button renders and toggles, ⌘K command palette still opens and searches correctly with the experience entries removed.
